'' A POINTER INTO A BOOLEAN, measured on fbc-modern 1.20 (2026-10-13): a run-time pointer is
'' fbc's 181 ('bo = p', 'return p'), 24 ('dim as boolean b = p', 'TakeBool( p )') and 20
'' ('cbool( p )') -- TKO0910, TKO0698 and TKO0890 here; tiko compiled all five. A pointer
'' CONSTANT (nullptr, 'cptr( any ptr, 0 )') is fbc's warning 5 only -- TKO0968 -- into a
'' boolean and into a narrow integer alike ('by = nullptr' was a false TKO0910 before), and
'' 'cbool( nullptr )' is silent. 'return p' from a function 'as long' is 181 too.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir %s
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: (37,5): error TKO0910: a pointer does not fit in a 'boolean'
'' EXPECT-OUT: (40,5): error TKO0910: a pointer does not fit in a 'long'
'' EXPECT-OUT: (42,1): error TKO0910: a pointer does not fit in a 'boolean'
'' EXPECT-OUT: (43,16): error TKO0910: a pointer does not fit in a 'boolean'
'' EXPECT-OUT: (44,11): error TKO0698: this argument does not convert to the parameter's type
'' EXPECT-OUT: (45,11): error TKO0890: 'cbool' cannot convert a 'long ptr'
'' EXPECT-OUT: (46,1): warning TKO0968: implicit conversion: a 'boolean' from a 'any ptr'
'' EXPECT-OUT: (47,1): warning TKO0968: implicit conversion: a 'byte' from a 'any ptr'
'' EXPECT-OUT: (48,1): warning TKO0968: implicit conversion: a 'long' from a 'any ptr'
'' EXPECT-OUT: (49,1): warning TKO0968: implicit conversion: a 'boolean' from a 'any ptr'
'' EXPECT-NOT: (31,
'' EXPECT-NOT: (32,
